// The Worker that serves the built page beside the Pages project `heroesims` (v1.0.1-S3, DL-94;
// DL-88 items 7 to 9, DL-92 items 4 and 6): Cloudflare Workers static assets, no script. `npm run
// deploy` uploads web/dist to it with `wrangler deploy --config wrangler.jsonc`, then to Pages
// (scripts/deploy.mjs). Its address is the Worker's name, then the account's workers.dev
// subdomain: `addresses.worker` in scripts/deploy.mjs, which the live check reads.
//
// - No `main`: the Worker is assets only. No `account_id`: the login supplies it, and none enters
//   the repository (INPUTS 7.9). No "$schema" path: wrangler comes by npx, never installed (DL-68).
// - `preview_urls` false: each preview or version URL would be another origin, with its own saves.
// - `not_found_handling` "none", set rather than left to the default: an unknown path is a 404.
//   Pages serves index.html for any path, but the page has one route, and a deeper path is broken
//   on both hosts anyway, since its script is ./assets/….
// - No "pages_build_output_dir": `wrangler pages deploy` warns that this file lacks it and ignores
//   the file, on every deploy; with it, `wrangler deploy` would refuse the file as a Pages one.
{
  "name": "heroesim",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-28",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "not_found_handling": "none"
  },
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": false
}
